  "title": "The community built beyond the prompt box",
  "summary": "October brought more community-built things to try, more image-model choices, and clearer paths through the API and Enter.\n\nHacktoberfest starters and a growing project directory brought map-to-city artwork, packaging mockups, an AI dungeon master, opposite-prompt images, and ReImagine’s image-editing workflow. App-hosting groundwork followed later in the month.\n\nGPT Image returned with editing support, Kontext moved to Azure Flux, and Seedream 4.0 joined the image models with a larger canvas. Nectar gained a high-quality gptimage option, while model listings and response headers made it easier to see what a request used.\n\nA new reference, image-model endpoints, and expanded quick-start examples made the API easier to navigate. Enter added Bearer-key support and a GET text endpoint for prompt-in-the-URL requests.\n\nDashboard and FAQ changes clarified keys, wallets, model access, and daily Pollen. The tier panel later added subscription details and read product names and daily amounts from Polar instead of hardcoded values.",
